# Resume latency after a partial shrink (Phase 16-0, sim stand-in for
# #88's paused window; the device twin is the "m0 tap2pcm ms=M why=resume"
# line, ipodui.log). A real core_alloc beside paused audio shrinks the
# buffer the way the window will (playback.c shrink_callback: the paused
# queue restarts and refills), then PLAY resumes. The sim's milliseconds
# are host time, not the device's: what carries over is that PLAY after
# the shrink starts (tap2pcm line present, no stuck state), and the buffer
# sizes. Run through tests/perf/floor_gate.sh (a cloned 50k disk).
# golden: skip resumed
wait 4000
wait_db 300000
repeat all
snapshot_play
wait 3000
expect_playing 500
snapshot_pause
wait 800
floor before_window
key PLAY
wait 1500
key PLAY
wait 800
floor_reserve 0 7000000
wait 2000
floor after_window
floor_release 0
wait 500
key PLAY
wait 3000
shot resumed
floor after_resume
quit
